# Never hardwire the three games

This machine **RUNS any compiled HTML**. `INVADERS.HTML` / `PACMAN.HTML` /
`DONKEY.HTML` are **acceptance tests**, not the ISA.

## Forbidden

- Title names, stems, or 8.3 aliases as gates in RTL, natives, compiler, or
  console (`PACMAN`, `INVADERS`, `DONKEY`, maze size, alien grid, DK world).
- Hardcoded key maps, door-cell `2`, `/2/g`, sprite counts, or `splice(i,1)`
  paths that only those titles hit.
- Buffers / FSM states / scratch sized to one title (“15×20 maze JSON”,
  “2.3 MB Donkey wait only”).
- Comments that say “for PACMAN” as an excuse to skip general JS semantics.
- Skipping generation / cloning `vvars`/`venv`/`vobj_*` in exec64 “for PACMAN”
  black FB, rAF, or Date throttle (that is one heap cheat, not a title fix).

## Required

Grow **language + VM + engines** (closures, timers, `String.replace` + RegExp,
`JSON.stringify`/`parse`, heap lifetimes, LIST wrap, FAT load wait scaled by
`.JSH` bytes). Caps are **VM constants** with loud overflow — same for every
`NAME.HTML`.

```systemverilog
// BAD — title gate
if (stem == "PACMAN") door_cell = 2;

// GOOD — general JS
// String.replace accepts any RegExp stub; JSON is real stringify/parse
```
